From 17640c9abece755cb63022354968cf1ad5a209bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 17:16:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add the credit system: rate card, provider meter, balances,
 enforcement
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replaces per-plan quotas with one credit balance every workspace draws from,
and moves metering to the provider boundary so it catches what the route-level
funding never saw.

Funding was reserved per user-facing action; money is spent deep inside the
pipeline. Everything between was invisible — the scene keyframes a video job
generates, the retry after one fails, the distinctness rerun after that, the
render a QA gate later rejects. recordUsage() only fires on success, so a
render the provider billed and then failed left no trace. The meter wraps the
provider call instead: a retry counts as two, a failure still records.

It also stores the provider's own token and USD figures, because Atlas bills
Seedance by output token rather than by second. The audit data in
reports/atlas-audit shows one reference-to-video request at 38,830 tokens and
sixteen at 324,000 — 8.3x apart on the same model. Recording only duration
hides the largest cost lever in the pipeline.

Three meter modes, and the order matters: shadow records and charges nothing,
enforce also debits, off disables. Land on shadow, reconcile the totals against
a provider invoice, then switch. Going straight to enforce charges from a rate
card nobody has checked.

Balances hold two buckets. Purchased credits never expire — expiring money
someone handed over reads as theft and the margin is already in the price.
Granted credits (plan allowance, signup, promo) do expire, and are spent FIRST
so an allowance is used rather than wasted while purchased credits drain.
Refunds land in purchased, so a refund for a failure that was never the
customer's fault carries no deadline.

Adds:
- credit_rates, credit_meter_settings, credit_meter_events, credit_accounts,
  credit_account_ledger, plan_settings.monthly_credits
- lib/creditRates, lib/meter, lib/creditAccounts, lib/creditQuote,
  lib/monthlyCreditGrant, lib/creditMigration
- Admin: rate card, meter report, migration dry-run and apply, per-tenant grant
- Tenant: GET /credits, GET /credits/quote, a header balance pill
- Monthly allowance on both gateway webhooks, idempotent per billing period

Metered at three chokepoints so far: image generation, scene keyframes
including retries, and video generation including provider failover. textGen,
imageEdit, ASR and voice cloning follow the same one-line pattern.

The meter never changes the outcome of a wrapped call: metering errors are
logged and swallowed, provider errors rethrow unchanged, and a failed mode
lookup falls through to running unmetered. In enforce the debit happens before
the provider call, so two concurrent generations cannot both spend the last
credit.

38 new tests. Full suite: 479 pre-existing failures before, 443 after.

